{"id":"assistant-021718a8-4e7e-50b8-9035-8b5536c754cc","sessionId":"b97259e6-0642-e6bd-dcdc-43d5836f5f11","turnId":"turn-5728423820c75cb5a8f53417cd90c78c","inputEntryId":"user-turn-5728423820c75cb5a8f53417cd90c78c-1","createdAt":1794273306808,"updatedAt":1794273306808,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\n1. **Added Prisma ORM** - Installed `prisma@7.10.1` and `@prisma/client@7.10.1` (latest stable from npm), plus `@prisma/adapter-pg` and `pg` for PostgreSQL connectivity.\n\n2. **Created Prisma schema** (`prisma/schema.prisma`) with:\n   - `User` model: id (autoincrement), email (unique), name (optional), posts (one-to-many)\n   - `Post` model: id (autoincrement), title (required), content (optional), published (default false), author relation\n\n3. **Created database tables** - Used `prisma db push` to create User and Post tables in the PostgreSQL database from `.env`.\n\n4. **Created `script.ts`** - Creates a user (Alice) with two posts (one published, one unpublished), then prints all users with their posts. Uses PrismaPg adapter and runs with `npx tsx script.ts`.\n\n5. **Created `prisma.config.ts`** - Configures the datasource URL from the environment.\n\n6. **Created `ANSWER.md`** - Documents everything that was done.\n\nAll files are in the project root. The script runs successfully and produces the expected output."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
